[$in title:["Templates"]]
[$in description:["Build Strings and typed sequences with template bodies, slots, child wrappers and control flow."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
listed = sync_navigation(sidebar_id)!
[section, $md:
    # Templates

    Use a template to put a name into a greeting, fill a card with content or
    produce a list from a loop. Square brackets enclose the construction. A
    colon opens its body. A text body produces a String.

    The Alpha compiler supports String templates. Typed sequence templates,
    including sequence slots and child wrappers, belong to the bracket design
    described in @../collections (Collections and maps).

    @#template-directives Find every formatter and structural directive in
    the @../template-directives (Template directives reference).
]

